WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.831
Lisa sat among the trees on the island, drawing.

2
00:00:03.832 --> 00:00:08.850
"Lisa! We need to leave," shouted Mom.

3
00:00:08.851 --> 00:00:11.417
"I’m coming," said Lisa.

4
00:00:11.418 --> 00:00:13.351
Lisa hurried to the boat.

5
00:00:13.352 --> 00:00:17.505
"I just finished my picture. Look."

6
00:00:17.506 --> 00:00:21.135
"Oh, that’s very nice," said Mom.

7
00:00:21.136 --> 00:00:23.770
"Is that you on the horse?"

8
00:00:23.771 --> 00:00:27.483
"No," answered Lisa sadly.

9
00:00:27.484 --> 00:00:30.090
"I don’t know how to ride a horse.

10
00:00:30.091 --> 00:00:36.236
This is Princess Sunapee and the eagle king."

11
00:00:36.237 --> 00:00:40.367
"It's a nice picture," said Grandma.

12
00:00:40.368 --> 00:00:44.545
"It’s also time to teach her to ride."

13
00:00:44.546 --> 00:00:50.068
"Lisa is too young to ride a horse," said Mom to Grandma.

14
00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:54.128
"Wow, what a day!" said Dad.

15
00:00:54.129 --> 00:00:57.581
"I’m exhausted," said Frank.

16
00:00:57.582 --> 00:01:02.538
"I guess it must be all the swimming and baseball."

17
00:01:02.539 --> 00:01:09.219
"I can’t wait to go to bed so I can put my eagle feather under my pillow," said Lisa.

18
00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:13.311
"I know it’ll work just as well as a tooth."

19
00:01:13.312 --> 00:01:17.741
Back at Grandpa’s house, Lisa talked to her brother.

20
00:01:17.742 --> 00:01:22.625
"Having a missing tooth feels strange," said Lisa.

21
00:01:22.626 --> 00:01:26.171
"You’ll get used to it," said Frank.

22
00:01:26.172 --> 00:01:30.629
"And the big ones in back feel the strangest."

23
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:32.825
"I’ll lose those too?

24
00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:36.511
Wow, that’s a lot of wishes."

25
00:01:36.512 --> 00:01:41.052
"Ah, don’t believe in those wishes too much," said Frank.

26
00:01:41.053 --> 00:01:43.530
"My wishes hardly ever came true.

27
00:01:43.531 --> 00:01:49.020
Instead you’ll just find a dollar under your pillow in the morning."

28
00:01:49.021 --> 00:01:52.918
"I don’t believe you," said Lisa.

29
00:01:52.919 --> 00:01:56.642
"You’ll see," Frank said, smugly.

30
00:01:56.643 --> 00:01:58.813
"The tooth fairy is getting old.

31
00:01:58.814 --> 00:02:02.286
She can’t grant as many wishes as she used to.

32
00:02:02.287 --> 00:02:04.415
She’ll give you a dollar instead.

33
00:02:04.416 --> 00:02:12.294
If you find a dollar under your pillow tomorrow, then you know that your wish isn’t going to come true."

34
00:02:12.295 --> 00:02:20.168
Lisa didn’t believe her brother because she knew that she was making a wish to the feather fairy and not the tooth fairy.

35
00:02:20.169 --> 00:02:24.760
Lisa carefully put the feather under the pillow of the bottom bunk.

36
00:02:24.761 --> 00:02:28.393
"Did you brush your teeth?" asked Mom.

37
00:02:28.394 --> 00:02:32.671
"Yes, Mom, we both did," said Lisa.

38
00:02:32.672 --> 00:02:38.311
"Mom, Frank said that the tooth fairy is too old to grant wishes anymore.

39
00:02:38.312 --> 00:02:41.548
Is that true, Mom?" asked Lisa.

40
00:02:41.549 --> 00:02:46.746
"No, but the tooth fairy can’t grant all wishes.

41
00:02:46.747 --> 00:02:49.804
Her magic is only as big as your tooth.

42
00:02:49.805 --> 00:02:57.061
If your wish is too big for her magic, she sometimes just leaves a dollar," answered Mom.

43
00:02:57.062 --> 00:03:00.630
"Oh," said Lisa, smiling.

44
00:03:00.631 --> 00:03:08.408
"I thought Frank was lying about the dollar, but I guess his wishes were just too big for the tooth fairy."

45
00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:12.902
"Yes, now go to sleep," said Mom.

46
00:03:12.903 --> 00:03:17.503
Before Lisa went to sleep, she wished as hard as she could.

47
00:03:17.504 --> 00:03:25.944
"Please, feather fairy, let me learn how to ride a horse tomorrow."

48
00:03:25.945 --> 00:03:30.666
"Get up, sleepy head," said Frank. It was morning.

49
00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:36.577
"Did the tooth fairy grant your wish or did she just leave you a dollar?" continued Frank.

50
00:03:36.578 --> 00:03:38.947
He reached under Lisa’s pillow.

51
00:03:38.948 --> 00:03:42.286
"No! Frank!" shouted Lisa.

52
00:03:42.287 --> 00:03:46.732
"See," said Frank, holding up the dollar.

53
00:03:46.733 --> 00:03:52.024
"The tooth fairy has no magic."

54
00:03:52.025 --> 00:03:54.770
At breakfast Lisa looked glum.

55
00:03:54.771 --> 00:03:56.570
"What’s the matter?

56
00:03:56.571 --> 00:04:01.917
Did the tooth fairy grant your wish?" asked Grandma.

57
00:04:01.918 --> 00:04:04.269
"No, not really.

58
00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:08.129
I got a dollar instead," answered Lisa.

59
00:04:08.130 --> 00:04:15.146
"Frank says that’s because the tooth fairy is old and her magical powers are weak.

60
00:04:15.147 --> 00:04:22.175
My mother said it was because my wish was too big, but my wish wasn’t too big.

61
00:04:22.176 --> 00:04:25.728
I guess Frank was right."

62
00:04:25.729 --> 00:04:30.616
"Hmm," said Grandma, thinking about the situation.

63
00:04:30.617 --> 00:04:37.451
"Being pretty old myself, I don’t think the tooth fairy’s magic is failing.

64
00:04:37.452 --> 00:04:43.079
If your wish isn’t too big, it might come true."

65
00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:49.550
"But why did I get a dollar instead of my wish?" asked Lisa.

66
00:04:49.551 --> 00:04:56.584
"Hmm, that’s a little more difficult to answer," said Grandma.

67
00:04:56.585 --> 00:05:01.810
"First, I think it was the tooth fairy that left the dollar.

68
00:05:01.811 --> 00:05:11.380
She came because she knew your tooth came out, but she found no tooth under your pillow.

69
00:05:11.381 --> 00:05:15.643
She can’t grant you a wish without a tooth.

70
00:05:15.644 --> 00:05:24.062
Second, because the feather is gone, I think the feather fairy granted your wish."

71
00:05:24.063 --> 00:05:29.113
"But my wish hasn’t come true," said Lisa.

72
00:05:29.114 --> 00:05:34.479
"Wishes don’t just come true like that," said Grandma.

73
00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:39.777
"Wishes happen only when they are supposed to happen."

74
00:05:39.778 --> 00:05:41.989
Lisa ate her cereal.

75
00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:44.126
She thought it made sense.

76
00:05:44.127 --> 00:05:49.203
Small magic works only when it can happen naturally.

77
00:05:49.204 --> 00:05:52.853
"Where’s Mom?" asked Lisa.

78
00:05:52.854 --> 00:05:57.333
"She’s in the barn," answered Grandma.

79
00:05:57.334 --> 00:06:02.241
"What are you looking at, Mom?" asked Lisa curiously.

80
00:06:02.242 --> 00:06:06.452
"Oh!" said Mom. "Come and sit beside me.

81
00:06:06.453 --> 00:06:08.779
I’d like to show you a few things.

82
00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:12.477
This is me when I was your age."

83
00:06:12.478 --> 00:06:19.423
"You?" shouted Lisa. "You rode in a horse competition?"

84
00:06:19.424 --> 00:06:25.507
"Yes, I did. I rode and I won," said Mom.

85
00:06:25.508 --> 00:06:30.390
"Wow, you were really lucky," said Lisa.

86
00:06:30.391 --> 00:06:33.735
"Lucky?" replied Mom.

87
00:06:33.736 --> 00:06:40.198
"Yeah, lucky to be able to ride horses every day," answered Lisa.

88
00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:51.063
"Oh," said Mom. "Yes, I was lucky to be able to ride horses every day and to have such a great riding instructor."

89
00:06:51.064 --> 00:06:54.926
"Who taught you how to ride?" asked Lisa.

90
00:06:54.927 --> 00:06:58.266
"My mother," she answered.

91
00:06:58.267 --> 00:07:06.649
"Now grab that bridle and that saddle, and I’ll show you how to ride," Mom ordered.

92
00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.925
"Now I’m lucky," said Lisa.

93
00:07:09.926 --> 00:07:12.577
"Lucky?" asked Mom.

94
00:07:12.578 --> 00:07:17.055
"Yeah, because now I’m learning how to ride from my mother.

95
00:07:17.056 --> 00:07:23.698
And I know that wishes can come true," said Lisa happily.

96
00:07:23.699 --> 00:07:36.466
"Yes, Lisa, wishes can come true," said Mom.

